Here's an attempt at a healer skill slot strategy.

The potentials are:

Expert at Healing school (4 slots), knife (5 slots),
quarterstaff (6 slots), dart (6 slots), unihorn (6 slots)

Skilled at dagger (3), short sword (3), club (3),
sling (3), shuriken (3)

Basic at scimitar (1), saber (1), mace (1), polearm (1),
spear (1), javelin (1), trident (1), bare handed (1) plus
whatever aritfacts arrive.

The healer artifact is the Staff of Aesculapius which may
be the best melee weapon in the game but is two handed.
Worth reserving slots at least up to Skilled (6).  Do
these enhancements after the Quest I think.

The only multifire option is dart so it seems worth maxing
that out for the machine gun effect.  Since there will be
dart traps early in the game it might be worth doing even
before there is a reliable way to bless them.

A healer might want to play a crysknife game otherwise
forget the knife and switch to daggers for the higher
damage and greater availability from monster initial
inventories.  More daggers appear in games than knives.

Unihorn is the best non-artifact weapon in the list,
especially with its non-weapon functions.

Most of the rest seem to be traps to waste slots on.

For a healer who does not avoid leveling up, I think
Healing to Expert (4), dart to Expert (6), dagger to
Skilled (3) leaves 16 slots to divide among knife,
quarterstaff and unihorn.  Bring all 3 up to Skilled
costs 8 leaving 8 to spend.  Hold a couple for arriving
artifacts and that tells me healers should go to Expert
at either unihorn or knife but not both.  If I did the
arthimatic right.



